---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = '19 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy notice | Fog Off" description="What Fog Off stores, why, for how long, and your rights.">
  <article class="wrap" style="padding-block:56px 0; max-width:800px;">
    <span class="pill">Privacy notice</span>
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem); letter-spacing:-0.03em; line-height:1.1; margin:16px 0;">How your data is handled</h1>
    <p class="draft"><strong>Draft, not yet reviewed by a legal adviser.</strong> Items shown as square brackets highlighted in yellow must be completed before launch. Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <div class="box">
      <strong>In short</strong>
      <ul>
        <li>By default <strong>nothing you type leaves your browser</strong>. Your answers and quotes are saved on your own device only.</li>
        <li>Sharing a report is <strong>optional</strong>, anonymous and banded. It never includes prices, your name, address, email, or free text.</li>
        <li>We publish only group figures, and only once at least 20 people have reported the same change.</li>
        <li>We do not sell data, show adverts or use tracking cookies.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>The controller of any personal data described here is <span class="todo">[YOUR NAME OR TRADING NAME]</span>, operating "Fog Off". Contact for privacy questions and requests: <span class="todo">[CONTACT EMAIL]</span>. We have not appointed a Data Protection Officer.</p>

    <h2>2. What we handle, why, and for how long</h2>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Why</th><th>Basis</th><th>Kept</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Your answers and quotes</strong> in the guided check, test plan, comparer and checklist</td>
            <td>To give you the tools and remember your progress</td>
            <td>Not received by us. Stored on your device only.</td>
            <td>Until you clear it (Start over, Start fresh, or clearing browser data)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>An optional shared report</strong>: age band, region, car age band, no-claims band, cover type, comparison site, percentage change for each test you choose, number of runs, baseline spread, and the week it arrived</td>
            <td>To build community findings that help other people</td>
            <td>Consent (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(a)), given by ticking the box and pressing Send. You can withdraw by deleting the report.</td>
            <td>24 months, then deleted. Backups can hold deleted rows for up to 30 days.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>A delete code hash</strong>: a one-way hash of the random code shown to you once</td>
            <td>So you can delete your own report without an account</td>
            <td>Same as the report</td>
            <td>Same as the report</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Report counters</strong>: how many reports were accepted this hour and day</td>
            <td>To stop floods of fake reports</td>
            <td>Not personal data (not linked to anyone)</td>
            <td>3 days</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Bot check</strong> (Cloudflare Turnstile), only when you open the share panel</td>
            <td>To stop automated abuse</td>
            <td>Legitimate interests: keeping the service secure and the data honest</td>
            <td>Handled by Cloudflare under its own terms. We receive only pass or fail.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Technical request data</strong> (such as IP address) when you visit</td>
            <td>To deliver and protect the website</td>
            <td>Legitimate interests</td>
            <td>Processed by Cloudflare on our behalf. We do not store IP addresses in our database, and we do not record them in reports.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>We do not ask for, and the form cannot accept, names, addresses, postcodes, dates of birth, email addresses, registration numbers, prices or free text in a shared report. Banded data is designed to be anonymous, but because several bands are combined we treat it as personal data to be safe.</p>

    <h2>3. Who receives data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> hosts the website and the report database and runs the bot check. It acts as our processor.</li>
      <li><strong>GitHub</strong> hosts the source code only. It receives no visitor or report data.</li>
      <li>We do not share, sell or rent data to anyone else, and we publish individual reports to no one.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Transfers outside the UK</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare operates a global network, including in the United States. <span class="todo">[Confirm: Cloudflare's data processing terms and the UK Addendum / International Data Transfer Agreement apply to our account.]</span></p>

    <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us to: tell you what we hold; correct it; delete it; restrict or object to our use of it; and, where we rely on consent, withdraw it at any time. You can also ask for a copy of data you provided.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fastest route:</strong> delete a report yourself with the code shown after sending (the "Delete a report I sent" box on the Share step, at the end of the Findings page).</li>
      <li><strong>Lost your code?</strong> Contact us at <span class="todo">[CONTACT EMAIL]</span>. Because reports are not linked to you, we may not be able to find yours. We will say so and explain what we can do. We reply within one month.</li>
      <li><strong>Complaints:</strong> you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk, helpline 0303 123 1113). We would like the chance to put things right first.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Browser storage (cookies and similar)</h2>
    <p>We use your browser's local storage to keep your own progress, because you asked us to save what you enter. The keys are <code>qg-advisor-v1</code>, <code>qg-whatif-v2</code>, <code>qg-compare-v1</code> and <code>qg-must-be-true</code>. They never leave your device and are not used for tracking or advertising. We set no cookies ourselves.</p>
    <p>If you open the share panel, a Cloudflare Turnstile script loads from Cloudflare and may use its own storage to tell people from bots. We load it only at that point. <span class="todo">[Adviser to confirm the PECR position for Turnstile and for local storage.]</span></p>

    <h2>7. Automated decisions and children</h2>
    <p>We make no automated decisions about you. The tools show general information from the data we hold. This service is not aimed at under-18s. If you are under 18, ask a parent or guardian before sharing a report.</p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this notice in a way that matters, we will update the date above and say what changed.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 34px 0 8px; }
  p, li { margin: 0 0 12px; }
  ul { padding-left: 20px; }
  .draft { background: var(--warn-soft); padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 12px; }
  .box { background: var(--accent-soft); border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px 18px; margin: 18px 0; }
  .box ul { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .tablewrap { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 0.88rem; min-width: 640px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 10px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  th { background: var(--surface-2); font-size: 0.78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--muted); }
  tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  code { background: var(--surface-2); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.85em; }
</style>
